hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19159","Qutayba ibn Said narrated to us, and Qutayba wrote it to me: Mujammi ibn Yaqub narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Mujammi, he said: It was said to Abd Allah ibn Abi Habiba: What did you witness of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had arrived when he was a young boy. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us one day to our mosque, meaning the mosque of Quba. He said: So we came and sat to him, and the people sat to him. He said: So he sat as long as Allah willed to sit, then stood to pray. So I saw him pray in his sandals."
"19160","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us: al-Attaf narrated to us: Mujammi ibn Yaqub narrated to me, from a youth of the people of Quba whom he reached as an old man, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us at Quba and sat in the courtyard of al-Ujum, and people gathered to him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked for drink and was given drink and drank, while I was at his right, the youngest of the people. So he handed to me and I drank. And I remembered that he prayed with us that day wearing sandals he did not remove."
"19161","Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us. Abd Allah said: And I heard it from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shayba. Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Habiba, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us and prayed with us in the mosque of Banu Abd al-Ashhal. So I saw him placing his hand in his garment when he prostrated."
